HFITS algorithm adaptations
Original authors: P. Dehghani and M. J. DiDomizio, Fire Safety Research Institute,
UL Research Institutes. The selected inverse energy balance and nominal material
law are adapted locally from HFITS and distributed under GPL-3.0; see LICENSE.
Adaptations: removal of GUI/file-format dependencies, vectorized numerical
evaluation, explicit public NPZ interfaces, and measured-collar target selection.
The selected source equations and numerical conventions are preserved.

Thermography observations
Matthew J. DiDomizio (2024), Heat Transfer and Fire Damage Patterns on Walls for
Fire Model Validation, dataset v1.0.0, UL Research Institutes / FSRI.
DOI: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10543089
License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Changes: extract an existing time/spatial window; retain stored Kelvin values;
convert coordinate arrays from inches to metres; repackage numeric arrays as NPZ.
Historical author irradiance estimates are separately labeled and are not truth.
